2026-04-20 21:58:57,289 INFO HTTP Request: POST http://localhost:8002/v1/chat/completions "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
AnswerChecker (to chat_manager):



Okay, imagine you have a LEGO set with instructions to build a specific model. 

* **Mitosis** is like making a *copy* of that LEGO set. You start with one set, and after mitosis, you have *two* identical sets, each with all the same pieces and instructions.  This is how your body cells grow and repair themselves - they make copies of themselves!

* **Meiosis** is a bit more complicated. It's like taking apart the LEGO set and shuffling the pieces around, then using those shuffled pieces to build *two* *new* models. These new models won't be exactly the same as the original, because some pieces have been mixed up.  This is how sex cells (sperm and egg) are made.  When a sperm and egg combine, they create a new individual with a mix of traits from both parents.

**Here's a simple table to summarize:**

| Feature        | Mitosis                                  | Meiosis                                  |
|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|
| Purpose        | Growth and repair                       | Production of sex cells (sperm and egg) |
| Number of cells | 2 identical daughter cells              | 4 unique daughter cells                 |
| Genetic makeup | Identical to parent cell                 | Different from parent cell and each other |


